    "result_text": "Each person's row now shows a Stern column, worked out as keel minus fathom. It shows n/a when keel is n/a, the same way the other columns built on keel do. `bin/e2e` passes.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Server** (`PersonView.java`): added a `stern` field to the person data the API returns. Its calculation sits next to `bow`, and I updated the class comment to describe it.\n- **Front end**: added `stern` to the `Person` type in `people.service.ts`, and a \"Stern\" column after \"Bow\" in `people-list.ts`, with the `data-testid=\"concept-stern\"` the test expects.\n\nFathom is keel plus momentum, so stern always works out to minus momentum. For example, Ada's momentum is 18, so her stern is -18.\n\nStern is calculated from existing fields, so the database, migrations and test seed/read-back endpoints are unchanged.",
